{"name":"Thiers-Issard razors","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Thiers_Issard_Le_Thiernois_with_Blonde_Horn_handle.jpeg/960px-Thiers_Issard_Le_Thiernois_with_Blonde_Horn_handle.jpeg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thiers_Issard_Le_Thiernois_with_Blonde_Horn_handle.jpeg","caption":"Thiers Issard Le Thiernois with Blonde Horn handle","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Thiers-Issard is a French maker of straight razors, listed by Wikipedia among Europe's best-known. Its razors are folding blades with a handle, used for wet shaving to leave the face smooth.","The appearance payoff is a close, clean shave for people who prefer it to cartridges or electrics. Forum users on T Nation have recommended the brand in threads about shaving."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["The blade is held at roughly 30 degrees and moved across the skin; the edge is kept aligned by stropping on leather and restored by honing on whetstones. Carbon steel is easier to hone but rusts more readily than stainless."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["An open blade can cut skin, and square or spike points can nick inexperienced users. Very thin hollow-ground blades flex and are unsuited to heavy beard growth. Some jurisdictions require barbers to use disposable-blade shavettes for hygiene."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Thiers_Issard_Le_Thiernois_with_Blonde_Horn_handle.jpeg/960px-Thiers_Issard_Le_Thiernois_with_Blonde_Horn_handle.jpeg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Thiers_Issard_Le_Thiernois_with_Blonde_Horn_handle.jpeg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Thiers Issard Le Thiernois w