24906199@N00/2235814900","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/163ea1fd-be35-4bc8-826f-e93fe5659028/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/7375/8980265035_b887a4053e_b.jpg","title":"Thiers Issard 3","license":"BY-NC-SA 2.0","creator":"jsj666","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/97153032@N08/8980265035","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/06328940-ba80-47b0-8e6b-465178bf4a9c/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/2856/8981460716_7812b72612_b.jpg","title":"Thiers Issard 5","license":"BY-NC-SA 2.0","creator":"jsj666","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/97153032@N08/8981460716","source":"Flickr"}],"links":{"studies":[],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"What's Underrrated?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/whats-underrrated/118818","site":"T Nation · 135 posts · 2008"},{"title":"Shaving: Best Blades?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/shaving-best-blades/120540","site":"T Nation · 40 posts · 2009"},{"title":"What Razor Do You Use?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/what-razor-do-you-use/130592","site":"T Nation · 32 posts · 2009"},{"title":"Tapered Shirts","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/tapered-shirts/121391","site":"T Nation · 24 posts · 2009"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Thiers Issard — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thiers_Issard"},{"title":"Straight razor - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straight_razor"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Grooming","chain":["Shave with a honed, stropped straight razor","Blade cuts hair close to the skin","A smooth, clean-shaven face"],"effect":"direct","text":"A well-kept straight razor produces a close shave, and users value it as a premium alternative to cartridge razors."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Thiers Issard","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thiers_Issard"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Thiers-Issard is a French straight razor maker. Wikipedia calls it one of Europe's best-known razor makers, noting that French makers such as Thiers Issard still use Sheffield silver steel and that it is noted for decorated blades and Damascus steel [1].","People use straight razors as a traditional route to a close shave. Interest in them revived after the 2012 film Skyfall featured a straight razor shave, according to Wikipedia [1]. On the bodybuilding forum T Nation, posters in 2008 and 2009 shaving threads named the brand, with one writing that nothing comes close to it [2][3]."],"infobox":[["Type","Straight (folding) razor"],["Origin","France"],["Notable features","Decorated blades, Damascus steel, Sheffield silver steel"],["Maintenance","Stropping and honing"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Straight razors have scales that protect the blade when folded and protect the user from accidental cuts. Blade width and point shape affect handling, and round points are recommended for beginners [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Maintenance","paras":["Stropping on leather keeps the edge aligned, while honing on whetstones restores sharpness. Carbon steel is easier to hone but rusts more readily; stainless resists rust but is harder to hone [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in grooming communities","paras":["In T Nation threads, one poster wrote that a Thiers Issard straight razor was the best, another listed owning one among underrated pleasures, and a third named it alongside Dovo [2][3][4]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Safety","paras":["Square or spike points can nick inexperienced users, and thin hollow-ground blades suit light beards [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Straight razor","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Straight_razor","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Shaving: Best Blades?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/shaving-best-blades/120540","source":"T Nation","year":2009,"type":"forum"},{"title":"What Razor Do You Use?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/what-razor-do-you-use/130592","sou